{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#721","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#721","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#721\",\"parent_revision\":\"e5ee7b924061216ef4139b511926326b8e3ae6e9\",\"root_revision\":\"28911bd5bbe416bdde98f82bd3b290f6ea537381d76f556c599c4d3c9b4d1231\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTask.bookend_type is typed as bare str instead of an enum. A typo like 't0-basline' would silently pass validation and produce a task invisible to BookendValidator (neither T0 nor TN). The field should use a StrEnum or Literal type constrained to the documented values ('t0-baseline', 'tn-verification'). BookendValidator already checks bookend_type values, but the model itself does not enforce valid values at construction time.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `Task.bookend_type` field location | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/task_format.py` |\\n| 2 | `BookendValidator` location and comparison logic | DERIVABLE | Grep `task_format.py` for BookendValidator |\\n| 3 | Valid bookend_type values | AVAILABLE | Item description: 't0-baseline', 'tn-verification' |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 clear improvement to type system, fully specified.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **sam bookend bookend_type enum validation** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review \u2014 SAM bookend validation implementation (followup-1)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature (typing improvement). Low complexity. Strengthens type safety without behavioral change. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `Task.bookend_type` field uses `BookendType(StrEnum)` with values `'t0-baseline'` and `'tn-verification'`, or `Literal['t0-baseline', 'tn-verification']`\\n- Pydantic model rejects invalid bookend_type values with a clear error at construction time\\n- `BookendValidator` updated to use `BookendType` enum values in comparisons\\n- Existing task files with valid bookend_type strings continue to load correctly\\n- `ty check` passes with no new suppressions\\n- Tests: at least one test asserts that invalid bookend_type raises `ValidationError`\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/task_format.py` \u2014 add BookendType StrEnum, update Task.bookend_type field and BookendValidator\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 add validation error test\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a SAM task author, I need `Task.bookend_type` to use a StrEnum or Literal type instead of bare `str` so typos like 't0-basline' fail at construction time rather than silently producing tasks that BookendValidator never sees.\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P696-sam-bookend-validation-followup-1.yaml | current | dh_migrate | 2026-03-24T16:35:39Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d8ff52cd01deb75cc89d7f468b5f9ba8603133fd0327c5d035865ccadab64a0c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgzGmw\"}"}